#: tips.cpp:3
msgid ""
"<p>Kalva comes with a nice set of plugins, providing the possibility to import "
"channellists from other applications.</p>\n"
"<p>Don't forget to <strong>save</strong> the imported channellist.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:9
msgid ""
"<p>If You used KTvApp (the successor of Kalva) You might want to reuse the old "
"configuration and channellists.</p>\n"
"<p>KTvApp stored it's channellists under "
"<strong>$KDEHOMEDIR/applnk/chlst</strong>. So You might want to type the "
"following commands into the console to make the channellists available for "
"Kalva and to reuse KTvApp's config in Kalva.</p>\n"
"<p><code>mv $KDEHOMEDIR/applnk/chlst $KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva/chlst"
"<br>\n"
"mv $KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva/* $KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva</code></p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:17
msgid ""
"<p>You can provide your channellist for other users.</p>\n"
"<p>KTvApp stores it's channellists under "
"<strong>$KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva/chlst</strong>. Get yourself an account at "
"www.kde-files.org and upload your channellist via the web interface.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:23
msgid ""
"<p>You can provide your hardware profile for other users.</p>\n"
"<p>KTvApp stores it's hardware profiles under <strong>"
"$KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva/hwprofile</strong>. Get yourself an account at "
"www.kde-files.org and upload your hardware profile via the web interface.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:29
msgid ""
"<p>You can provide your quality profiles for other users.</p>\n"
"<p>KTvApp stores it's quality profiles under <strong>"
"$KDEHOMEDIR/apps/kalva/qprofile</strong>. Get yourself an account at "
"www.kde-files.org and upload your quality profiles via the web interface.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

